1.0.0
source: https://github.com/lina-silvera/marketing (doc-engine/)

The generic layout engine in this folder — engine.css, page-a4.css,
page-a5.css, _page-template.css, build.sh, brand.py, compress.py and
insert-toc.lua — is a copy of doc-engine at the version above.

Improvements flow ENGINE REPO -> HERE, never the other way. If this
project needs behaviour the engine lacks, change it in the engine repo,
bump its VERSION, and re-copy the files here. Patching the copy in place
forks it, and the next update will either clobber the patch or conflict
with it silently.

Project-specific files in this folder are NOT part of the engine and are
owned here: project.toml, anywair-skin.css, assets/ and INSTRUCTIONS.md.

KNOWN DIFFERENCES from doc-engine 1.0.0, as split:

  page-a4.css, page-a5.css, _page-template.css, compress.py
      identical.

  build.sh, brand.py
      diverged BY DESIGN. The engine versions take their paths as
      arguments (--project, and the project-folder name) to suit the
      engine's engine/ + scripts/ layout; the copies here keep the
      original flat single-folder paths. Re-copying these two needs the
      path handling reconciled — they are not a drop-in replacement.

  engine.css
      one comment line only; no rule differs.

  insert-toc.lua
      the engine has a FIX this copy does not: an H2 with no H1 above it
      is promoted to a top-level Contents entry instead of being dropped.
      Without it, a guide whose only H1 is its title produces an empty
      Contents page. No guide here is affected — all are numbered from
      H1 down — and the change was verified to leave this project's
      manual byte-identical. Worth taking on the next sync anyway.
